    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5673" root="جزأ" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَزْءٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُزْءٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  It is said by El-Khattábee to
be a name for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُطب</span> [app. meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُطْبٌ</span>, i. e.
<i>Green,</i> or <i>fresh, pasture</i> or <i>herbage,</i> (see 1 and
4,)], with the people of El-Medeeneh; and occurs
in a trad.; but the reading commonly known is
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جرو</span>. (TA.)

